    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d684">

                <pb facs="0821" n="811" sameAs="frus:frus1944v02/pg811"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.70/10–544: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-10-06T00:00:00-04:00">October 6,
                            1944—midnight</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>8188. For Hooker, Allison and Moats from Berle and Plakias.<anchor n="47"
                        xml:id="d684-f1"/> Reference penultimate paragraph Embassy’s 8366 October 5.
                    Department feels same principle should govern participation of Rumanian Control
                    Commission at EITO Conference as applied to ACC for Italy, SHAEF et cetera,
                    namely, participation as observers only.</p>
                <p>However the Department feels that representation of Control Commission for
                    Rumania should await full establishment of the Commission and the naming by the
                    full Commission of a delegate as observer. <pb facs="0822" n="812"
                        xml:id="pg812"/> (We have no objection in principle to the Soviet delegate
                    being this observer, but feel that the appointment should be made by the
                    Commission itself.) [Berle and Plakias.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d684-f1" n="47" xml:id="d684-f1-content">
                <p>John N. Plakias, special assistant, Office of Transportation and
                    Communications.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
